  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math> be the roots of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;be the roots of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Then the roots of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;are :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "non-real complex numbers",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "real and both negative",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "real and both positive",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "real and exactly one of them is positive",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math> be the roots of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>So sum of roots will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;and product of roots will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math></p><p>And also given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;are roots of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>So sum of roots will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And similarly product of roots will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Now adding equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;{as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></math>}</p><p>Now putting the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>17</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> are the roots, both roots are real and negative.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}